# Commit Message Format

This repo uses **Conventional Commits** enforced by `commitlint` with `@commitlint/config-conventional`.

## Rules

| Rule | Limit |
|------|-------|
| Header (first line) | max **100** characters total (type + scope + subject) |
| Body lines | max **200** characters per line |
| Subject | must not be empty |
| Type | must not be empty, must be one of the allowed types |

## Format

```
type(scope): subject

body (wrap lines at 200 chars max)
```

### Allowed Types

`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`

### Allowed Scopes

**Apps:** `web`, `app`, `api`, `docs`, `email`

**Packages (@eleva/*):** `ui`, `auth`, `db`, `billing`, `accounting`, `scheduling`, `calendar`, `notifications`, `workflows`, `flags`, `audit`, `encryption`, `ai`, `crm`, `compliance`, `observability`, `config`, `eslint-config`, `typescript-config`

**Sprint scopes:** `s0`–`s8`, `s1-a`, `s1-b`, `s2-a`, `s2-b`, `s3-a`, `s3-b`, `s4-a`, `s4-b`, `s5-a`, `s5-b`, `s0.1`–`s8.16`

**Cross-cutting:** `ci`, `deps`, `release`

Scope is optional. Omit it for changes spanning multiple areas.

## Examples

```
fix(auth): forward request headers in proxy middleware composition
```

```
feat(scheduling): add weekly availability rules with timezone support

Implements the availability engine that computes open slots from
weekly rules minus calendar busy-time. Supports per-rule timezone
and date-range overrides.
```

```
chore: update turbo.json globalEnv with new billing vars
```

## Body Wrapping

If the body exceeds 200 characters on a single line, break it into multiple lines. Use blank lines to separate paragraphs.
